#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:29
msgid "In 4.10 there is a single panel-wide option for configuring the number of rows in the panel. Some plugins (e.g. *launchers*) fit a single row, while others, like window buttons are allowed to occupy full width of the panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:31
msgid "![A horizontal panel with a number of rows set to three][img-panel-rows]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:33
msgid "Deskbar Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:35
msgid "The panel features a new configuration called a *deskbar* mode. In the deskbar mode the panel is aligned vertically, just like in the vertical mode, but the plugins are laid out horizontally. With multiple rows, it allows creating wide vertical panels suitable for wide-screen setups."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:37
msgid "![A panel in Deskbar mode with a number of rows set to five][img-panel-deskbar]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:39
msgid "Actions Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:41
msgid "Session plugin from the xfce4-session package has been merged with a rewritten *actions* plugin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:43
msgid "![Action plugin in a menu mode (left), and in a button mode (right)][img-panel-actions]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:45
msgid "Window Buttons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:47
msgid "The *window buttons* plugin no longer expands, which makes the plugin positioning more flexible. In order to restore the previous behavior please add a transparent *separator* plugin with the **Expand** option enabled just behind the window buttons plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour410.md:49 content/about/tour412.md:105
#: content/about/tour414.md:55 content/about/tour416.md:41
#: content/about/tour418.md:71 content/about/tour46.md:67
#: content/about/tour48.md:9
msgid "File Manager *(thunar)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:51
msgid "There are few visual changes in this release of Thunar. The window has less padding and the position of the status bar has been adjusted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour410.md:53 content/about/tour46.md:33
msgid "Session Manager *(xfce4-session)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:55
msgid "The *session manager*'s settings dialog has a button for clearing the saved session (no more `rm -r ~/.config/sessions`). Xfce4-tips has been removed and the session manager can now lock the screen before suspending or hibernating the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:57
msgid "Applications Autostart"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:59
msgid "Another noticeable change is the way GNOME and KDE compatibility works. Compatibility check boxes only enable services, which have to be started before other applications (*gnome-keyring* and *gconf* for GNOME and *kdeinit* for KDE). All other autostart applications are available from **Applications Autostart**, but they are listed using an italic font and not enabled by default in order to distinguish them from Xfce applications. Unlike in previous versions of Xfce, compatibility services can be started independently from each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:61
msgid "![Applications, which are not a part of Xfce, are listed using an italic font][img-session-autostart]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour410.md:63 content/about/tour412.md:63
#: content/about/tour46.md:85 content/about/tour48.md:73
msgid "Settings *(xfce4-settings)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:65
msgid "Settings Daemon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:67
msgid "Xfce 4.8 used two processes for applying settings: `xfce4-settings-helper` and `xfsettingsd`. In 4.10 they have been merged into xfsettingsd, which now handles all system settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:71
msgid "The new *settings manager* groups configuration dialogs in categories and allows you to search for their names or descriptions. Most of the dialogs are also now embedded in the settings manager window (this was a compile-time option in Xfce 4.8)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:73
msgid "![The settings manager with icons grouped by category and a search filter applied][img-settings-manager]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:75
msgid "Settings Editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:77
msgid "The *settings editor* no longer collapses the entire tree when you edit a property (this is because it now reloads a single cell rather than the whole tree). Most properties can now be edited in-place, making it easier to quickly adjust settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:79
msgid "Using settings editor you can also monitor changes of settings in a selected channel. Right-click on a channel in the main window, and select **Monitor** to display the monitor window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:81
msgid "![Settings editor with an open channel monitor, while editing a property in-place][img-settings-editor]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:83
msgid "MIME Type Editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:85
msgid "In the last couple of years, many people were asking for a tool to manage their file type associations. The new *MIME type editor* does just that. It allows you to easily assign a default application to a file type, see your changes and reset them to default settings when necessary. Note that it does not allow you to change the system MIME Type definitions (add or remove types and change icons)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:87
msgid "![MIME types matching a pattern and a menu for selecting a default application][img-settings-mime]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:89
msgid "Mouse and Touchpad"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:91
msgid "The *mouse and touchpad* dialog is capable of handling basic Synaptics and Wacom properties in the GUI. A settings daemon running in the background handles all kinds of device properties, as documented in the [mouse settings](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/mouse) wiki."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:93
msgid "![Synaptics touchpad settings in the mouse and touchpad dialog][img-settings-mouse]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour410.md:95 content/about/tour412.md:73
#: content/about/tour418.md:65 content/about/tour420.md:277
msgid "Appearance Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:97
msgid "In 4.10 you can drag and drop a tarball with a downloaded theme onto the *style* or *icon* list. Xfce will attempt to extract and install the files into the `~/.themes` or `~/.icons` directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour410.md:99 content/about/tour412.md:55
#: content/about/tour418.md:47 content/about/tour46.md:9
msgid "Desktop Manager *(xfdesktop)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:101
msgid "Although the initial plan for Xfce 4.10 was to integrate desktop handling in Thunar, we have decided not to do it at this time yet. Meanwhile, Xfdesktop has gained support for single-click operation, automated background image cycling and thumbnail rendering."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:103
msgid "![Desktop with image thumbnails and support for single-click operation][img-xfdesktop]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:105
msgid "Xfdesktop is now shipped with a new default background image."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour410.md:107 content/about/tour412.md:9
#: content/about/tour418.md:213 content/about/tour46.md:43
msgid "Window Manager *(xfwm4)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour410.md:109
msgid "Xfwm4 can now tile a window when you drag it to the edge of the screen. This feature is optional and is disabled by default. In such a case windows can still be tiled using a keyboard shortcut. Another improvement is a better theming support and cursor key navigation in the tab window (Alt+Tab)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/tour412.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.12 tour"
msgstr "prehliadka Xfce 4.12"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:7
msgid "This tour will introduce you to new major features of Xfce 4.12. It only covers improvements made on the surface; for the full list of changes, see the [changelogs](/download/changelogs/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:11
msgid "Window Switcher Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:13
msgid "The window manager's Alt+Tab dialog is now fully themeable and also gained two new modes: a 'List' mode and a 'Window Preview' mode. Furthermore users use their mouse to click/select the window they want to give focus to."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:15
msgid "![The traditional dialog is fully themable now][img-tabwin-simple-crop]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:17
msgid "The List mode of the Alt-Tab dialog."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:19
msgid "![List mode of Alt-Tab, showing all window titles][img-tabwin-list-crop]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:21
msgid "The Window Preview mode shows thumbnails of windows' content alongside their icon. Activating the compositor is a prerequisite for this mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:23
msgid "![Window thumbnails][img-tabwin-preview-crop]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:25
msgid "Tiling, Zooming, Client-side Decorations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:27
msgid "Support for Client-Side Decorations (CSDs) has been improved. They now properly snap to screen and panel borders, and tile correctly, even with shadows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:29
msgid "![Gtk3 apps with their decorations drawn by the client][img-xfwm4-csd]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:31
msgid "Window tiling mode was improved by providing support for corner-tiling, and a new zooming mode was added using Alt + Mouse Wheel."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:33
msgid "![Drag and drop a window to a corner to tile it][img-xfwm4-tiling-small]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:35
msgid "HiDPI Support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:37
msgid "In order to better support modern hi-resolution screens, two new Xfwm4 themes were added (hdpi, xhdpi)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:41
msgid "Intelligent Hiding"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:43
msgid "The panel can now intelligently hide itself when a window is dragged near it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:45
msgid "![Oh what is this window??][img-panel-shown]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:47
msgid "![Don't come closer!][img-panel-shown-stack]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:49
msgid "![Hah! Now you don't see me!][img-panel-hidden]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:51
msgid "Gtk3 plugins"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:53
msgid "Infrastructure was added to be able to load Gtk3 plugins alongside Gtk2 plugins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:57
msgid "The desktop has a new wallpaper settings dialog with many new options and better multi-monitor support. Drag the dialog to the display or workspace where you want to change the wallpaper."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:59
msgid "![Better multi-monitor support][img-xfdesktop-properties-multiworkspace]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:61
msgid "Uncheck 'apply to all workspaces' to set a different wallpaper for each workspace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:65 content/about/tour418.md:59
#: content/about/tour420.md:287
msgid "Display Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:67
msgid "Support for multi-monitor use was vastly improved in the display settings dialog. Upon connecting a new display, a quick setup popup offers some of the most-used modes for users to quickly change their layout."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:69
msgid "![Configure multiple displays][img-xfce4-display-settings-twoscreens]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:71
msgid "![Choose your layout when plugging in a new display][img-xfce4-display-layout]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:75
msgid "The appearance dialog now showcases previews for styles and icons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:77
msgid "![Gtk style preview][img-xfce4-appearance-settings-style]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:79
msgid "![Icon theme preview][img-xfce4-appearance-settings-icons]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour412.md:81 content/about/tour414.md:69
#: content/about/tour416.md:67
msgid "Power Manager *(xfce4-power-manager)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:83 content/about/tour414.md:71
#: content/about/tour414.md:85
msgid "Panel Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:85
msgid "A new panel plugin was created which allows you to quickly control your screen brightness, either via the menu or by simply using your mouse's scroll wheel over the plugin. The plugin's menu also shows all other connected devices with a power status, e.g. bluetooth keyboards or wireless mice. It still offers quick access to the presentation mode, which inhibits your screensaver for as long as the option is active."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:87
msgid "![The plugin's menu allows users to control screen brightness and check on the remaining uptime their battery provides.][img-xfpm-plugin-crop]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:89 content/about/tour414.md:49
msgid "Settings Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:91
msgid "The settings dialog was completely restructured (separating button/lid events from system and display behavior) and offers a clearer way of setting your preferences."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:93
msgid "![Configure what action to take when certain buttons are pressed or the laptop lid is closed][img-xfpm-prefs-general]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:95
msgid "![Configure what to do when the user is inactive or battery is drained][img-xfpm-prefs-system]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:97
msgid "![Manage display power management][img-xfpm-prefs-display]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:99
msgid "![Display information on all connected devices][img-xfpm-prefs-devices]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:101
msgid "When light-locker is available, you can control its settings directly via the power manager."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:103
msgid "![Setup light-locker integration][img-xfpm-prefs-security]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:107
msgid "Tab Support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:109
msgid "A long-awaited feature was added: you can now open multiple folders in the same Thunar window."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:111
msgid "![Browse multiple directories][img-thunar-tabs]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:113
msgid "Thunar now displays the remaining free space with a bar in a folder properties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:115
msgid "![Freespace bar][img-thunar-freespace]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:117
msgid "And you can select multiple files to see their properties at once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:119
msgid "![Multiple File Properties][img-thunar-multifiles-props]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour412.md:121
msgid "Goodies"
msgstr "Goodies"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:123
msgid "There have been lots of improvements to our goodies, and some new and shiny applications have been added by new contributors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:125
msgid "Alternative panel menu plugin *(xfce4-whiskermenu)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:127
msgid "The whisker menu is an alternative to the traditional menu plugin, showing favourites, allowing to search through existing apps and much more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:129
msgid "![Browse through categories][img-whiskermenu-default]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:131
msgid "![Search for an application][img-whiskermenu-search]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:133
msgid "Task Manager *(xfce4-taskmanager)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:135
msgid "The task manager got a revamped user interface, a filter and also supports Gtk3 now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:137
msgid "![Show processes as a tree][img-taskman-tree]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:139
msgid "![Filter processes by name][img-taskman-filter]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:141 content/about/tour414.md:91
msgid "Media Player *(parole)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:143
msgid "Parole's UI was totally redone in Gtk3. It now supports multiple video backends, makes more efficient use of your resources and contains a few novel plugins."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:145
msgid "![Watch videos][img-parole]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:147
msgid "The media controls are now contained in a slide-over overlay (with a configurable timeout)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:149
msgid "![Listen to music][img-parole-audio]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour412.md:151
msgid "Text Editor *(mousepad)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:153
msgid "Mousepad was totally rewritten, gained a settings dialog and now supports Gtk3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:155
msgid "![New mousepad settings][img-mousepad-prefs]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour412.md:157
msgid "A note on Xfce's portability"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour412.md:159
msgid "All but one of those screenshots were taken on machines running OpenBSD -current, a good proof that Xfce is still portable and friendly to all Unix systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/tour414.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.14 tour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:7
msgid "This tour will introduce you to new major features of Xfce 4.14. It only covers improvements made on the surface; for the full list of changes, see the [changelogs](/download/changelogs/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:9 content/about/tour416.md:17
#: content/about/tour418.md:53
msgid "Settings Manager *(xfce4-settings)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:11
msgid "Color Profiles Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:13
msgid "A new dialog for setting [color profiles](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/4.14/color) for monitors, printers and scanners was introduced. It acts as a frontend to various daemons that talk directly to colord, e.g. saned (scanners), cupsd (printers) or xiccd (monitors)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:15
msgid "![The new color profiles dialog][img-color-profiles]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:17 content/about/tour416.md:29
msgid "Display Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:19
msgid "Several improvements were made to the [display dialog](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/4.14/display). Apart from tweaks to the user interface to make the interaction more intuitive (introducing display numbering, showing a primary indicator with quick access to panel, notification and desktop settings etc.) a feature to save and restore complete display profiles was added. If a single profile exists for a setup, the Xfce settings daemon will automatically enable it. If multiple profiles exist, it will pop up the minimal dialog and offer all profiles in addition to the previously available pre-sets (internal only, mirror, extend and external only)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:21
msgid "![The primary indicator][img-display-general]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:23
msgid "![The display profile list][img-display-advanced]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:25
msgid "![The improved minimal dialog - in this case only showing one profile only which never happens anymore now ;)][img-display-minimal]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:27
msgid "Accessibility"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:29
msgid "One [accessibility](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-settings/4.14/accessibility) feature that people coming from other desktop environments or operating systems were still missing is to set a (custom) keyboard shortcut (by default: Super+F1) to visually locate the mouse pointer. This feature was added in Xfce 4.14."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:31
msgid "![The mouse pointer location animation][img-locate-mouse]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:35
msgid "General: Icon size"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:37
msgid "A new feature that we introduced in the [panel](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-panel/4.14/start) is being able to control the icon size of all plugins. ('All' may not be technically correct, as not all plugins support the new API as of now, but now they *can*. Plus the Window buttons plugin is an exception, because libwnck doesn't allow anything other than 16px or 32px.) This means setups that were previously impossible, because icons would upscale automatically according to size-steps hard-coded in the panel, are now possible (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:39
msgid "![A 32px tall panel with 16px icons][img-panel-iconsize]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:41
msgid "Window buttons: Grouping"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:43
msgid "Grouping was improved in the [Window buttons plugin](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-panel/4.14/tasklist), both functionally (by improving the matching and icon-finding) and visually by providing a new group indicator that is less likely to clash with window titles containing an enumeration in brackets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:45
msgid "![The new group indicator (two terminal windows)][img-panel-group]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:47
msgid "Session *(xfce4-session)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:51
msgid "As soon as a [session](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-session/4.14/preferences) has been saved a new tab is dynamically added to the settings dialog displaying all saved sessions and allowing to delete one or all of them. This should make it way more discoverable for users if they actually have saved sessions that influence the startup behavior - previously this had to be checked manually in the filesystem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:53
msgid "![The settings dialog after saving a session][img-session-saved]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:57
msgid "Pathbar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:59
msgid "Up to Xfce 4.12 [Thunar](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/thunar/4.14/start) offered two options for the pathbar/locationbar. The best of both worlds has now been mixed into one powerful pathbar, featuring both clickable breadcrumbs (i.e. folders), an easily accessible way to hand-type a path as well as an improved look."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:61
msgid "![Thunar's new pathbar][img-thunar-pathbar]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:63
msgid "Folder Thumbnailer"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:65
msgid "Same as on the Desktop you can now save an image with the name 'folder.jpg' in a folder and get it displayed as its icon in the File Manager. Note: [Please read the docs](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/tumbler/available_plugins#customized_thumbnailer_for_folders) on how to set this up (if your distribution hasn't enabled it by default)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:67
msgid "![Thunar's new folder thumbnails][img-thunar-folder-jpg]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:73
msgid "The [Power Manager's panel plugin](https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfce4-power-manager/4.14/panel-plugin) supports symbolic icons now and uses the standard UPower icon names (making it more compatible with all icon themes). It also shows an indicator if applications inhibit power management functions like suspend (when power is low) or display dimming (after a defined timeout)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:75
msgid "![Parole's video playback is inhibiting power management][img-xfpm-inhibitors]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:77
msgid "Notification Service *(xfce4-notifyd)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:79 content/about/tour44.md:123
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "Nastavenia"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:81
msgid "Several new features have been added in Xfce's [Notification service](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/notifyd/start), including a notifications log, the possibility to disable notifications per application, a global 'Do Not Disturb' mode, which inhibits all notifications, and finally a new animation ('slide out')."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:83
msgid "![The new notification animation 'slide out'][img-notifyd-slideout]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:87
msgid "Furthermore a new panel plugin was added which provides quick access to both the 'Do Not Disturb' mode as well as the log of recent notifications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:89
msgid "![The new panel plugin][img-notifyd-panel]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:93
msgid "Mini Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:95
msgid "[Parole](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/parole/start) now features a 'Mini Mode', where the interface is simplified to just display the album artwork and can be positioned over other windows without getting in the way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:97
msgid "![Just right-click anywhere in the player window to select 'Mini Mode'...][img-parole-normal-mode]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:99
msgid "![Afterwards, enjoy a truly minimalistic playback experience!][img-parole-mini-mode]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:101
msgid "Screensaver *(xfce4-screensaver)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour414.md:103
msgid "A Modern Locking Experience"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:105
msgid "The new Xfce [Screensaver](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/screensaver/start) provides a configurable lockscreen experience. You can selectively toggle the lock screen and screensaver, and all Xscreensaver themes are supported (with configuration options) out of the box. If you prefer a blank screen, Xfce Screensaver also includes a blank screen option with DPMS integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:107
msgid "![The new lock screen, sharing styles with LightDM GTK+ Greeter for a consistent experience.][img-saver-dialog]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:109
msgid "![Make it your own. Xfce Screensaver supports a multitude of configuration options.][img-saver-preferences]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:111
msgid "Terminal *(xfce4-terminal)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:113
msgid "Lots and lots of features have accumulated in the [Terminal](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/terminal/start) over the last years. Amongst them 'Undo Close Tab' and 'Close Other Tabs' functionality (similar to web browsers), 'Copy Input to All Tabs', 'Set Title Color' (allows to customize tab text color), 'Save Contents' (saves tab contents to a file), an 'Unsafe Paste' dialog (which prevents the terminal from auto-executing pasted text as a command) and support for zooming. Finally when closing a tab or window, there is a new check for running processes which prevents accidentally closing a terminal that is running a process."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:115
msgid "![Zooming, 'Save Contents' and much more!][img-terminal]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour414.md:117
msgid "Screenshooter *(xfce4-screenshooter)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:119
msgid "The Xfce [Screenshooter](https://docs.xfce.org/apps/screenshooter/start) gained several notable features, amongst others seeing the size of the screenshot while dragging, moving the selection with the mouse and better [imgur](https://imgur.com) integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour414.md:121
msgid "![I can drag and move the screenshot area, whoop whoop!][img-screenshooter]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/tour416.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.16 tour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:7
msgid "This tour will introduce you to new major features of Xfce 4.16. It only covers improvements made on the (user-visible) surface; for the full list of changes, see the [changelog](/download/changelogs/4.16/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour416.md:9
msgid "Visual identity: New icons and palette"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:11
msgid "In order to make Xfce shine a little more out of the box and to strengthen its visual identity we created new icons for all of our core applications and based them on a shared palette to ensure consistency. We also set some further (implicit) design constraints, loosely following Adwaita's principles."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:13
msgid "![The Xfce palette][img-palette]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:15
msgid "![New upstream Xfce icons, coming in many sizes for sharp appearance][img-upstream-icons]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:19
msgid "The Settings Manager itself received a visual refresh of its filter box, which can now be hidden permanently. At the same time the search capabilities of the filter box were improved by searching the descriptive 'Comments' part of each dialog's launcher (aka [.desktop](https://specifications.freedesktop.org/desktop-entry-spec/desktop-entry-spec-latest.html)) file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:21
msgid "![Visually cleaner, more powerful filter box][img-settings-manager]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour416.md:23 content/about/tour418.md:163
msgid "Default Applications"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:25
msgid "This new dialog represents a merger between the previously available 'Mime Settings' and the 'Preferred Applications' dialogs. Consolidating both in one place means users have an easier time setting default applications to handle certain file types."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:27
msgid "![The new Default Applications dialog][img-default-applications]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:31
msgid "To better support high-density displays - which come in various sizes and densities - we added fractional scaling based on the RandR extension of X11. Furthermore the preferred mode of a display is now marked with an asterisk and aspect ratios are shown along display resolutions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:33
msgid "![Fractional scaling support][img-display-dialog]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour416.md:35
msgid "Keyboard Shortcuts"
msgstr "Klávesové skratky"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:37
msgid "In order to make things easier for our users we added more default keyboard shortcuts out of the box, for instance for window tiling or to open Thunar. The keyboard shortcuts dialog itself was also visually updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:39
msgid "![Visually updated keyboard shortcuts dialog][img-keyboard-shortcuts]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:43
msgid "In Thunar's copy and move dialogs users can now easily pause the respective file operation. Furthermore support for queued file transfer, remembering view settings per folder and support for transparency in Gtk themes was added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:45
msgid "![Thunar can now pause copying/moving files][img-thunar-copy]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:49
msgid "The panel received quite a few noteworthy updates, an animation for autohide and intellihide, a new 'Status Tray' plugin that combines both legacy Systray item support with modern StatusNotifier item support, dark mode support, launchers showing additional actions on right-click, window buttons offering to 'Launch a new instance...' and much more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:51
msgid "![Dark mode enabled in the panel's settings dialog][img-panel-dark]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:53
msgid "![The new statustray plugin][img-panel-statustray]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:55
msgid "![Autohide animation][img-panel-autohide]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:57
msgid "![Launch a new instance!][img-panel-launch]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour416.md:59
msgid "About Dialog *(xfce4-about)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:61
msgid "Not only was the Xfce tab reworked to be more visually appealing and easily parsable, a separate tab showing basic information about the user's system was also added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:63
msgid "![About Xfce][img-about-xfce]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:65
msgid "![About System][img-about-system]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:69
msgid "The settings dialog of the power manager was cleaned up and shows either 'on battery' or 'plugged in' settings as opposed to both in a huge table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour416.md:71
msgid "![Power Manager settings][img-powermanager]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/about/tour418.md:0
msgid "Xfce 4.18 tour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:7
msgid "This tour will introduce you to new major features of Xfce 4.18. It only covers improvements made on the (user-visible) surface."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:9
msgid "Check the full [Xfce 4.18 changelog](/download/changelogs/4.18/) for a detailed list of changes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour418.md:11
msgid "Widget Library *(libxfce4ui)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:13
msgid "Filename Input Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:15
msgid "XfceFilenameInput is a comfortable widget for filename input, which was added in order to prevent invalid filenames at an early stage and to give detailed feedback on the concrete problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:17
msgid "![XfceFilenameInput - trailing whitespaces][img-xfce4ui-new-file-dialog1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:19
msgid "![XfceFilenameInput - slash][img-xfce4ui-new-file-dialog2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:21
msgid "Generic Shortcut Editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:23
msgid "This widget is a shortcut editor which was introduced in order to have a graphical interface to modify component-specific shortcuts. Currently, it is only used inside Thunar, Xfce4-terminal and Mousepad, though other components might follow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:25
msgid "![XfceShortcutsEditor in Thunar][img-xfce4ui-shortcuts-editor]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/about/tour418.md:27
msgid "Thumbnail Service *(tumbler)*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:29
msgid "Some performance improvements for the pixbuf-thumbnailer and the scheduler were done. As well now there are multiple overwrite options for the desktop-thumbnailer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:31
msgid "There is now support for the thumbnail sizes x-large and xx-large, which are very useful for high resolution displays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:33
msgid "Tumbler and Thunar now support shared thumbnail repositories, like described in the freedesktop.org thumbnail specification. This feature can be used to produce thumbnails for a folder in advance, directly located near the pictures. Like that, the thumbnails don't need to be re-generated for each individual user."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:35
msgid "For more information on shared thumbnails, check the [related blog post](http://users.uoa.gr/~sdi1800073/sources/xfce_blog03.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:39
msgid "The DateTime and the Clock plugins provided overlapping functionality. In order to prevent parallel development, they have been merged into a single plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:41
msgid "![The new 'Clock' panel widget][img-panel-clock1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:43
msgid "The new Clock plugin received a new binary time mode now and provides a sleep monitor. Here's a screenshot of all possible layouts which are: Analog, Binary, Digital, Fuzzy and LCD."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:45
msgid "![All possible Clock Modes][img-panel-clock2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:49
msgid "Like in Thunar, the 'Delete' menu entry in the context menu can now be hidden."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:51
msgid "In order to don't mess the desktop by accident on pressing 'rearrange desktop icons', the user is asked for confirmation now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:55
msgid "The search entry for xfce4-settings-manager was a bit simplified. Now it will always be shown, without any slider or button."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:57
msgid "![xfce4-settings-manager - the search entry is always shown][img-settings-main-dialog]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:61
msgid "xfce4-display-settings got some minor improvements and the possibility to decide what to do when new displays are connected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:63
msgid "![xfce4-display-settings - minor improvements][img-settings-display]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:67
msgid "On selecting a new theme, there is now the option to automatically set a matching xfwm4 theme, if available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:69
msgid "![xfce4-appearance-settings - toggle to set matching Xfwm4 theme][img-settings-appearance]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:73 content/about/tour420.md:171
msgid "List View"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:75
msgid "For directories, the count of containing files can now be displayed in the size column. It is now possible to add a 'file creation date' column, and the 'configure columns' dialog can be opened with a right-click on any column head."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:77
msgid "![Thunar - List View - Preferences][img-thunar-listview1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:79
msgid "![Thunar - List View - File count and file creation date][img-thunar-listview2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:81
msgid "Image Preview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:83
msgid "Finally, an image preview side pane has been added to Thunar. No, wait, actually two of them! You can choose to either use the 'embedded' mode which will take no extra space, but hide parts of the left side pane. Or you can go for the 'standalone' mode, which will use a separate pane on the right and display as well some basic information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:85
msgid "![Thunar - Embedded Image Preview][img-thunar-preview1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:87
msgid "![Thunar - Standalone Image Preview][img-thunar-preview2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:89
msgid "Undo and Redo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:91
msgid "It is now possible to undo basic file operations and to redo them. Undo and Redo can be used for 'move', 'rename', 'trash', 'link' and 'create' operations. Per default, a history of the last 10 operations is stored, though the history length is configurable. Whenever an Undo/Redo is triggered, a notification with few details will be shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:93
msgid "![Thunar - Undo and Redo][img-thunar-undo-redo]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:95
msgid "File Highlight"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:97
msgid "Files now can be highlighted by setting the background and the filename to different colors. This can be done via an additional tab, located in the 'properties' dialog. The view menu provides a checkbox in order to enable/disable the feature. Once enabled, files now can be shown in all the colors of the rainbow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:99
msgid "![Thunar - File Highlight Options][img-thunar-hightlight1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:101
msgid "![Thunar - Highlighted files in List View][img-thunar-hightlight2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:103
msgid "![Thunar - Highlighted files in Icon View][img-thunar-hightlight3]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:105
msgid "For more information on file highlight, check the [related blog post](https://elessar-space.blogspot.com/2022/08/gsoc22-file-highlighting-in-thunar.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:107 content/about/tour420.md:90
msgid "Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:109
msgid "It is now possible to customize the toolbar according to your personal needs! An additional dialog has been added for that purpose, on which the visibility and position of specific items can be managed. As well custom actions, which appear for folders can be used in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:111
msgid "When the menubar is hidden, an additional toolbar button which can be used to show the menu will be displayed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:113
msgid "![Thunar - Toolbar with all configurable Elements][img-thunar-toolbar1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:115
msgid "![Thunar - Toolbar Configuration Dialog][img-thunar-toolbar2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:117
msgid "![Thunar - Show Menubar button][img-thunar-toolbar3]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:119
msgid "For more information on the configurable toolbar, check the [related blog post](http://users.uoa.gr/~sdi1800073/sources/xfce_blog10.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:121 content/about/tour420.md:177
msgid "Split View"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:123
msgid "Thunar now provides the option to use split panes. The pane separator can be moved, and its position will be stored. Via a xfconf setting, it is as well possible to have a vertical split."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:125
msgid "![Thunar - Split Panes][img-thunar-splitpanes]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:127 content/about/tour420.md:115
msgid "Statusbar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:129
msgid "The status bar style was tweaked and '|' is now used to separate entries. Furthermore, it is now possible to customize it by using the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:131
msgid "![Thunar - Statusbar Customization][img-thunar-statusbar]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:133
msgid "Recursive Search"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:135
msgid "Thunar has now the possibility to search recursively, directly inside Thunar itself. The search is done in a separate thread and search results are added rapidly into a List View. A new row 'Location' shows where the search results are located, and the context menu provides the option 'Open Item Location' in order to travel there quickly. The preferences dialog provides an option to limit recursive search to local folders, or to disable it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:137
msgid "![Thunar - Recursive Search][img-thunar-search1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:139
msgid "![Thunar - Recursive Search Preferences][img-thunar-search2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:141
msgid "For more information on the recursive search feature, check the [related blog post](http://users.uoa.gr/~sdi1800073/sources/xfce_blog04.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:143
msgid "Recently used Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:145
msgid "Recently used files now can be accessed in the side pane. Like for the 'Recursive Search' feature, the new 'Location' row can be used in List View. Additionally, for 'Recent' a new row 'Recency' can be added to sort the files by their latest usage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:147
msgid "![Thunar - Recently Used Files][img-thunar-recent]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:149
msgid "For more information on 'Recent' in Thunar check the [related blog post](http://users.uoa.gr/~sdi1800073/sources/xfce_blog02.html)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:151
msgid "Bookmark Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:153
msgid "In order to keep the 'Go' menu compact, bookmarks have been moved into a separate, new 'Bookmarks' menu. The menu item 'add Bookmark' was rather hidden in the 'send to' menu in Thunar 4.18. As part of the new 'Bookmarks' menu, it is more prominent now."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:155
msgid "![Thunar - Bookmarks Menu][img-thunar-bookmarks]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:157
msgid "Trash directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:159
msgid "With the new release, the trash directory provides an info bar which gives easy access to `Empty Trash` and 'Restore' functionality. When using List View, a 'Date Deleted' column will be shown, so that the files can be sorted by deletion date. Via context menu, it is now possible to select 'Restore and Show' in order to automatically open a new tab in the folder of the restored file(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:161
msgid "![Thunar - Trash Infobar and Date Deleted Column][img-thunar-trash]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:165
msgid "The management to set/unset default applications for specific mime types was improved. The context menu got a dedicated item 'Set Default Application' which will open the 'ApplicationChooserDialog' with 'use as default' preselected. The dialog now has a section 'Default Application' in order to make clear which default application currently is set. If you want to remove applications from the list, right click it and select 'forget association'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:167
msgid "![Thunar - Context Menu Entry to set Default Application][img-thunar-default-application1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:169
msgid "![Thunar - Revamped Application Chooser Dialog][img-thunar-default-application2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:171 content/about/tour420.md:147
msgid "Custom Actions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:173
msgid "It is now possible to arrange custom actions in cascading submenus. Just enter the same submenu name for a custom action in order to place it into the same menu. If you require multiple menu levels, you can achieve that by using '/' in the path of the 'Submenu' entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:175
msgid "![Thunar - Custom Action Submenu][img-thunar-uca-submenu1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:177
msgid "![Thunar - Custom Action Configuration Dialog][img-thunar-uca-submenu2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:179 content/about/tour420.md:227
#: content/about/tour420.md:355
msgid "Preferences"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:181
msgid "The thumbnail settings in the preferences dialog got grouped together, and meanwhile it is possible to limit the file size for which thumbnails should be generated. That should mitigate possible performance issues by preventing thumbnail generation for huge video files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:183
msgid "![Thunar - Thumbnail Preferences][img-thunar-preferences1]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:185
msgid "File transfer operations optionally can use *.partial~ as an intermediate file now. After a transfer operation, there is now the option to verify the file checksums in order to make sure that no single bit got corrupted. Note that the checksum feature will require some extra time during copy when activated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:187
msgid "![Thunar - File Transfer Preferences][img-thunar-preferences2]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:189
msgid "For more information on the new file transfer options, check the [related blog post](https://dev.ikx.kr/GSOC-5th/)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:191
msgid "A checkbox was added in order to allow running shell scripts. In Thunar 4.18 it only was possible to change that behavior by changing a hidden setting. Use that option with caution!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:193
msgid "![Thunar - Script Execution Preferences][img-thunar-preferences3]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:195
msgid "There is now the possibility to restore tabs on startup, and to show the full directory path in the tab title."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:197
msgid "![Thunar - Tab and Window Preferences][img-thunar-preferences4]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: content/about/tour418.md:201
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/about/tour418.md:203
msgid "Application Finder got support for the 'PrefersNonDefaultGPU' property, which is useful for systems with hybrid graphic cards."
